   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the radius of convergence of the power series \\( \\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{5^{2n}(x-2)^{n}}{n^{3}} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         1,
         25
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "For the ratio test, \\( \\left|\\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}\\right| = \\frac{25 n^{3} \\left|{x - 2}\\right|}{\\left(n + 1\\right)^{3}} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Multiply",
               25,
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  [
                     "Power",
                     "n",
                     3
                  ],
                  [
                     "Abs",
                     [
                        "Add",
                        "x",
                        -2
                     ]
                  ]
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Power",
               [
                  "Add",
                  "n",
                  1
               ],
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "As \\( n \\to \\infty \\), the limit of this ratio is \\( 25 \\left|{x - 2}\\right| \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            25,
            [
               "Abs",
               [
                  "Add",
                  "x",
                  -2
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The series converges when \\( 25 \\left|{x - 2}\\right| < 1 \\), that is, when \\( \\left|x - 2\\right| < \\frac{1}{25} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            25
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The radius of convergence is \\( R = \\frac{1}{25} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            25
         ]
      }
